* t37crclo.a -- CONF68K test t36: F$CRC over a whole valid module leaves the* documented CRC constant -- low word.** Claim (DOCS/claims.md): "An easier method of checking an existing module's* CRC is to perform the calculation on the entire module, including the* module CRC. The CRC accumulator contains the CRC constant bytes if the* module CRC is correct. The CRC constant is defined in sys.l and usr.l as* CRCCon. Its value is $00800FE3." (Technical Manual, F$CRC, page 1 - 25),* with "The CRC accumulator must be initialized to $FFFFFFFF before the* first F$CRC call for any particular module" from the same page.** The module under test is this one: F$Link finds it in the module directory* and hands back its header in a2, M$Size at offset $04 is "the overall* module size in bytes, including header and CRC", and a module that OS-9* agreed to load necessarily has a correct CRC -- so the constant must come* out. That makes the test independent of any particular data, which is the* point: the manual fixes no CRC for any given byte string, only this* constant for a whole correct module.** $00800FE3 is 8392675, which does not fit the report's six-digit field, and* the suite prints OVRFLW rather than a plausible-looking truncation. So the* constant is checked as two honest 16-bit observations: t36 takes the* high word ($0080 = 128) and this one the low ($0FE3 = 4067). Together they pin* the whole value; neither reports a number it did not observe.** Promoted from test/68k-live-verification/batch4-01.a, which called F$CRC* and printed whatever came back -- no expected value, so nothing could* disagree with it.*Prgrm set 1Objct set 1ReEnt set $80Type_Lang set (Prgrm<<8)+ObjctAttr_Rev set (ReEnt<<8)+1IWrite set $8AFExit set $06FLink set $00FUnLink set $02FCRC set $17MSize set 4*EXPECT set 4067* psect t37crclo,Type_Lang,Attr_Rev,0,2048,startstart lea myname(pc),a0 moveq #0,d0 trap #0 dc.w FLink bcs.w setuperr movea.l a2,a3 move.l MSize(a3),d0 movea.l a3,a0 move.l #$FFFFFFFF,d1 trap #0 dc.w FCRC bcs.w setuperr move.l d1,d5 movea.l a3,a2 trap #0 dc.w FUnLink moveq #0,d6 move.w d5,d6 cmpi.l #EXPECT,d6 beq.w ispass bra.w isfail* use verdict.i use report.i*myname dc.b "t37crclo",0idstr dc.b "RESULT t37 ",0passtr dc.b "PASS",0failstr dc.b "FAIL",0errstr dc.b "ERROR",0obsstr dc.b "  obs=",0expstr dc.b " exp=",0descstr dc.b "  F$CRC over a whole module leaves CRCCon, low word $0FE3",0 ends